Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: extend buffered LAN forwarding to GDM4

Keep PPE hardware offload and extend the board opt-in to direct GDM4 LAN
destinations. Preserve WAN, other GMAC, WDMA and SOE rules. Only fresh
flows change; no module selector, register writes or live FOE mutations.
The existing DT opt-in name is retained for board compatibility.
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -456,13 +456,14 @@
 			val |= FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB2_PSE_PORT, pse_port) |
 			       FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB2_DSCP, dsfield) |
 			       AIROHA_FOE_IB2_PSE_QOS;
-			/* Slow DSA egress can exhaust the SRAM descriptor queue
-			 * under bursts from a faster ingress. Use buffered DRAM
-			 * hardware forwarding on boards with this limitation.
-			 * Direct GDM and WDMA output paths are unchanged.
+			/* Use buffered hardware forwarding for opted-in DSA and
+			 * GDM4 LAN destinations. SRAM forwarding can amplify TCP
+			 * retransmissions under bursts on affected boards.
+			 * WAN, other GDM and WDMA paths remain unchanged.
 			 */
 			if (airoha_is_lan_gdm_dev(dev) &&
-			    (dsa_port < 0 || !eth->dsa_dram_forwarding))
+			    (!eth->dsa_dram_forwarding ||
+			     (dsa_port < 0 && port->id != AIROHA_GDM4_IDX)))
 				val |= AIROHA_FOE_IB2_FAST_PATH;
 			if (dsa_port >= 0)
 				val |= FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB2_NBQ,
